[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
IMPLEMENTATION items record concrete mechanisms present in the current source
tree. The statements describe the code as written, including deliberately
unfinished target ports and the current verification boundary. Code references
are recorded as File relations and, where useful, repeated in comments for
readability. These records are descriptive implementation notes rather than
additional behavioral requirements.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Build, configuration, and common failure handling

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-001
TITLE: Configuration defaults and compile-time guards
STATEMENT: >>>
``include/zef_config.h`` supplies defaults for reactor slots, topic count,
message-pool count, state depth, mailbox capacity, tick type, pool alignment,
assertion mode, and claim-counter type. Preprocessor checks constrain the
configured ranges for the main limits. Static assertions check the alignment
and the selected integer widths. ``ZefMaxAlign`` provides the maximum scalar
alignment used by the default pool alignment expression on the supported host
compilers.
<<<
