[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-011
TITLE: Message lifecycle and claim accounting
STATEMENT: >>>
Dynamic Messages begin with one creator reference. A consuming Mailbox post or
topic publication transfers that reference to the framework and nulls the
sender pointer. Retain increments the reference counter, release decrements it, and the final release returns the block
to its originating pool. Static Messages bypass claim changes and pool
reclamation. Checked mutable and read-only accessors verify the lifecycle and,
for typed access, the exact payload size.
<<<
