[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-061
TITLE: Timer-owned messages and base claims
STATEMENT: >>>
Payload timer initialization allocates and copies one private dynamic Message
for the Timer. Expiry retains one claim per queued delivery, while the Timer
keeps its base claim until terminal cancellation. Stopping or one-shot expiry
leaves the base claim in place so the Timer can be armed again. Cancellation
unlinks the Timer, removes matching private Message entries, and releases the
retained base claim. Topic timers use an embedded zero-payload static Message
and do not use pool claims.
<<<
COMMENT: Code references: src/zef_timer.c; src/zef_mailbox.c.
