[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Ports, optional preemption, and verification

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEF-IMP-070
TITLE: Port callback boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
``ZPort`` is a public callback structure containing critical-section entry and
leave, reschedule request, and idle operations. Kernel and TopicTable code use
the critical callbacks when a Port is available. The current host test defines
no-op callbacks directly in ``tests/zef_smoke_test.c``; there is no standalone
host-port source file.
<<<
